# @godxjp/ui

> A Japanese-enterprise React design system: {{components}} components, {{tokens}} design tokens,
> {{rules}} cardinal rules. This file is the entry point for AI agents. Catalog version {{version}}.

If your client can run a process, do not read these files — run the MCP server instead
(`npx @godxjp/ui-mcp@{{version}}`). It is searchable and version-locked. These files exist for agents
that can only fetch URLs.

## Start

- [START-HERE.md]({{raw}}/START-HERE.md): the whole contract — the four rules, the token override model, a page that passes review. Read this first; it is self-contained.
- [index.json]({{raw}}/index.json): version, counts, and the URL of every file.

## Catalog

- [patterns-index.json]({{raw}}/patterns-index.json): {{patterns}} whole-task patterns (name, tagline, tags). Start here when the task is a TASK — "build a settings page" — then fetch `patterns/<name>.json` for complete code.
- [components-index.json]({{raw}}/components-index.json): {{indexSize}} — all {{components}} components as name, group, tagline, plus `absorbed`: the names that do NOT exist and map to it (`Combobox` → `Select`).
- [components/&lt;Name&gt;.json]({{raw}}/components/Select.json): one file per component ({{perComponentSize}}). Read the index, then fetch only the ones you chose — this is the selective route, and the reason you do not need the blob.
- [components.json]({{raw}}/components.json): {{componentsSize}} — every entry in one file. Most URL fetchers truncate a response this size without saying so; prefer the per-component files.
- [tokens.json]({{raw}}/tokens.json): every design token with its value, the reason it exists, and its `tier` — {{tokensFoundation}} `foundation` seeds (`--primary`, `--background`, `--radius`: set these when you are handed a brand), {{tokensSemantic}} `semantic` roles, {{tokensComponent}} `component` knobs.
- [vocabulary.json]({{raw}}/vocabulary.json): the controlled prop vocabulary — which prop name means what, across every component.
- [rules.json]({{raw}}/rules.json): {{rules}} cardinal rules.
- [anti-ai-tells.json]({{raw}}/anti-ai-tells.json): {{tells}} shapes that make generated UI look generated, each with its fix.

## Pinning

Every URL above tracks `main`. To pin to the release a project actually installed, swap `main` for
the tag: `.../godx-jp/godxjp-ui/v{{version}}/agent/...`. A catalog that does not match the installed
package describes props that are absent, or hides props that are present, and says nothing either way.

{{pinnedCaveat}}
